 1. So v ranges from 1001 down to 1. Hmm, so v=0 is never used in the loop. Let me redo.\n\nk ranges 0 to 1000. v = 1001 - k ranges 1001 down to 1.\n\ndelta for value v: 2*posSum[v] - cnt[v]*(N+1) = 2(v+1) - 1003.\n\nans[k+1] = sum over v from 1001 down to 1001-k of (2v + 2 - 1003).\n\nLet m = k+1. ans[m] = sum_{v = 1002-m}^{1001} (2v - 1001).\n\nSum of 2v from v = 1002-m to 1001: 2 * (sum from 1002-m to 1001) = 2 * (m terms, average = (1002-m + 1001)/2) = 2 * m * (2003 - m)/2 = m(2003 - m).\n\nThen subtract 1001*m: ans[m] = m(2003 - m) - 1001m = m(2003 - m - 1001) = m(1002 - m).\n\nSame as before. ans[m] = m(1002 - m) for m = 1..1001, and ans[0] = 0. \n\nSo the output is:\n0\n1001\n2000\n2997\n...\nk(1002-k)\n...\n1001\n\nI need to compute all 1002 values: k*(1002-k) for k=0 to 1001.\n\nLet me compute each:\nk=0: 0\nk=1: 1*1001 = 1001\nk=2: 2*1000 = 2000\nk=3: 3*999 = 2997\nk=4: 4*998 = 3992\nk=5: 5*997 = 4985\nk=6: 6*996 = 5976\nk=7: 7*995 = 6965\nk=8: 8*994 = 7952\nk=9: 9*993 = 8937\nk=10: 10*992 = 9920\nk=11: 11*991 = 10901\nk=12: 12*990 = 11880\nk=13: 13*989 = 12857\nk=14: 14*988 = 13832\nk=15: 15*987 = 14805\nk=16: 16*986 = 15776\nk=17: 17*985 = 16745\nk=18: 18*984 = 17712\nk=19: 19*983 = 18677\nk=20: 20*982 = 19640\nk=21: 21*981 = 20601\nk=22: 22*980 = 21560\nk=23: 23*979 = 22517\nk=24: 24*978 = 23472\nk=25: 25*977 = 24425\nk=26: 26*976 = 25376\nk=27: 27*975 = 26325\nk=28: 28*974 = 27272\nk=29: 29*973 = 28217\nk=30: 30*972 = 29160\nk=31: 31*971 = 30101\nk=32: 32*970 = 31040\nk=33: 33*969 = 31977\nk=34: 34*968 = 32912\nk=35: 35*967 = 33845\nk=36: 36*966 = 34776\nk=37: 37*965 = 35705\nk=38: 38*964 = 36632\nk=39: 39*963 = 37557\nk=40: 40*962 = 38480\nk=41: 41*961 = 39401\nk=42: 42*960 = 40320\nk=43: 43*959 = 41237\nk=44: 44*958 = 42152\nk=45: 45*957 = 43065\nk=46: 46*956 = 43976\nk=47: 47*955 = 44885\nk=48: 48*954 = 45792\nk=49: 49*953 = 46697\nk=50: 50*952 = 47600\nk=51: 51*951 = 48501\nk=52: 52*950 = 49400\nk=53: 53*949 = 50297\nk=54: 54*948 = 51192\nk=55: 55*